{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace-service/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T21:07:30.818881Z","id":"5a650ad8dcb1f137d9060977c3288a6433ad2f6f15c573308908a3484298f232","body":{"detail":"The job table is memory. RemoteWorkspace::ask (crates/clax-bot-remote/src/remote.rs) sends a request up to three times, so a POST whose answer was lost, followed by a service restart and the next attempt, finds no key and starts the command again. A step executed again is safe: it goes through resume_exec, which only polls and answers shell_interrupted on 404. The window is a restart inside one call's retries. Keeping each begun key in a file, and answering a key begun before the restart as interrupted, would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":207},"end":{"line":235},"content_hash":"97d1baff3374c86e5e09daa52d51d39efff023eec594fb76b2580df4c924113a"},"summary":"A restart between two sends of one POST /v1/jobs runs the command twice","tags":["review","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace-service/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T21:07:30.818929Z","id":"c088d81815735f7790f869ca5c3499c4b1ba119ad2ae613a65987b71bee8bca1","body":{"detail":"Service::end aborts every running job so that ContainerWorkspace::finish does not wait on the slot lock, a proposal's as well as a command's. Dropped between its push and Forge::open, a proposal leaves the branch on the remote with no pull request, and the finished run cannot come back to finish it. A command has no such cost, as the container is destroyed next. Letting a proposal past its push run to its end would need a mark from ContainerWorkspace::propose that the host's Stop then waits on.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":250},"end":{"line":269},"content_hash":"55097382c0b5bcd3153d2b0978cfafda1bed7f1343a7b7631bb90b1581292b19"},"summary":"Ending a run aborts a proposal wherever it stands, which can leave a pushed branch with no pull request","tags":["review","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace-service/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T22:15:01.863325Z","id":"5ef8c97883142f77098a3293e516bd97084dc469807e99fb789e23935bd45567","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"A command's key is synced to workspace-jobs.log before it starts (crates/clax-bot-workspace-service/src/begun.rs), and Service::take answers a known key with no job as shell_interrupted. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot-workspace-service:integration, jobs::a_restart_between_two_sends_of_one_post_runs_the_command_once passes and failed before the change.","supersedes":"5a650ad8dcb1f137d9060977c3288a6433ad2f6f15c573308908a3484298f232","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace-service/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T22:15:02.010196Z","id":"3e7beb457a5046b3747cf27055173974787537d8a61bc181c93d1534395e5f48","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Service::end aborts commands at once and waits for a begun proposal up to Limits::proposal_settle; DELETE answers within routes::ANSWER_WITHIN while the ending goes on. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot-workspace-service:integration, jobs::stop_lets_a_proposal_under_way_open_its_pull_request_then_answers and jobs::stop_answers_within_its_bound_and_the_proposal_still_finishes pass and failed before the change. A proposal past that bound is still aborted: jobs::a_proposal_stuck_past_the_bound_is_aborted_and_the_run_ended.","supersedes":"c088d81815735f7790f869ca5c3499c4b1ba119ad2ae613a65987b71bee8bca1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace-service/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T22:15:02.155220Z","id":"1855d6099a0748d2bfc3b78d522d1236948d328975577194106141d7f95865af","body":{"detail":"Service::snapshot takes seq as the greatest of the time now and what it gave before, which holds within a process. Across a restart it rests on the clock alone. A host keeps the snapshot with the greatest seq (crates/clax-bot-remote/src/remote.rs), so a clock set back leaves it on old offers until the clock catches up or MAX_SNAPSHOT_AGE_MS passes. Keeping the greatest seq in a file would close it, at a write per change.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":285},"end":{"line":299},"content_hash":"63d666500faad133b61d5a1f406255b41d999b4b1c08722fd836bf0d9822a2bd"},"summary":"Snapshot::seq is the wall clock, so a clock set back across a restart makes a host ignore new snapshots","tags":["review","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace-service/src/previews.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T22:15:02.155260Z","id":"ef1a3b389dde30e439f9e1c8e231e1ab96b16423ca5f00489cfd4809e9c5feed","body":{"detail":"PreviewLog::add keeps a word in memory when the save fails, the host hears it from memory, and each GET /v1/previews saves again. A restart in that window drops the word. The ledger's wait then answers for it: taken up while it has time, or told as missed once past its end, which can say no preview came up when one did. The window is a full disk and a restart together, before the host's next poll.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":90},"end":{"line":106},"content_hash":"fd359ffee8a86bb656e73a1ad7a27d68b6da8134a435de2560b130bfef73b4ea"},"summary":"A preview's word the disk would not take is lost if the service restarts before the next save","tags":["review","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace-service/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T23:16:35.120406Z","id":"60a2ab383e899e1bbd4618991fa4a8267ad823c848c46eeb55008261b19a2941","body":{"detail":"Service::end reads Entry::pending and, finding no mark, aborts the job. The proposal task may write the mark on another worker thread between that read and the abort, reach the push, and be dropped there. The outcome is a branch with no pull request and no answer, the failure the mark exists to avoid, in a window of a file read. Closing it takes a handshake inside ContainerWorkspace::propose (crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/workspace.rs): propose asks to pass, under a lock end also takes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":506},"end":{"line":512},"content_hash":"54f69afeaefabb41590144e7a86bb37c004246e804bfac973a3417ec9958bd42"},"summary":"Stop reads a proposal's mark from the ledger and then aborts, so a proposal crossing the mark in between is cut at its push","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-workspace-service/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-06T23:16:35.120434Z","id":"62fd77730bb904d1cc363ff8a6481e52a4e26e68375dcf21016716a5dff5031d","body":{"detail":"LEDGER_DIR copies home.join(\"workspace-runs\") from crates/clax-bot-workspace/src/config.rs, since ContainerWorkspace does not expose its ledger. If the two part, Ledger::read answers a default Entry with no pending, so every proposal reads as short of its push and Stop aborts it, past the push too. Tests share the name through World::ledger_dir (crates/clax-bot-workspace-service/tests/fixture.rs), so they would not catch it. An accessor on ContainerWorkspace answering whether a proposal is past its push would remove the copy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"06643c9436e9a169403bbc6eb1d76142d9d0757d02751348f2c9317a04bba03c"},"summary":"The service finds its workspace's ledger by repeating a directory name, and a mismatch aborts every proposal on Stop","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
